            <ArticleTitle>Bifurcate popliteus tendon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>638-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 18-year-old woman suffering from lateral patellar pain and subluxation underwent knee arthroscopy. The arthroscope revealed a bifurcate appearance of the popliteus tendon. This is the first report of this appearance at arthroscopy. The bifurcate popliteus tendon is a normal variant finding with no clinical significance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
